    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1034">

                <pb facs="0899" n="887" xml:id="pg887"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/3955: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-17T13:00:00-05:00">June 17, 1940—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 17—1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. Department’s 89, June 13, 8 p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d1034-f1"/> In
                    conformity with a recent telephone conversation I suggested to President Vincent
                    in a conversation this morning at which Pixley was present to resume
                    construction at the $160,000 per month rate. President Vincent enthusiastically
                    approved.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
